# .dev.vars.example — secret definitions for the Deploy to Cloudflare button
#
# The Deploy to Cloudflare button reads THIS file (not .dev.vars) to display
# a secret-input form to the user during deployment setup.
# Docs: https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/platform/deploy-buttons/
#
# ── Format ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# KEY=default_or_placeholder_value  # optional inline comment shown in the UI
#
# ── How to use locally ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Copy this file to .dev.vars and fill in real values:
#   cp .dev.vars.example .dev.vars
# .dev.vars is gitignored and is loaded automatically by `wrangler dev`.
#
# ── How to set in production (manual deploy) ──────────────────────────────────
#   npx wrangler secret put <KEY>
#
# ── Secrets for this Worker ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Uncomment and set a value if you want to require callers to pass a shared
# token in the X-Proxy-Token request header (simple bearer-style auth).
# Leave commented out if you rely solely on the ALLOWED_ORIGINS allowlist.
#
# PROXY_AUTH_TOKEN=replace-with-a-strong-random-value
